# Python 2.7.18 (2020-04-19) grammar: py2-int-print subset over the slice's tokens.
# @version 1
# PARTIAL: parses only the py2-int-print subset below; everything else is a parse error; see code/grammars/python/README.md.
# source_ref: https://github.com/python/cpython/tree/v2.7.18
# source_sha: 8d21aa21f2cbc6d50aab3f420bb23be1d081dac4
# evidence: Grammar/Grammar blob 4c3f33da32d5ca202b3e5549032e6c09e9784a6f; Grammar/Tokens blob -;
#   Parser/tokenizer.c blob 89666611940cf84c0a6e88ac7c365b134e9c5a26; Lib/keyword.py blob 69794bda8c879a098a2adaef5e4bcee32f8683c8
# basis: reviewed against the tag's own syntax files (LANG84 phase 7c slice 1). Tokens follow tokenizer.c tok_get (decimal [1-9][0-9]* or a single 0; octal, hex and `L` suffixes are not lexed) and PyToken_OneChar/TwoChars/ThreeChars (45 operators), and keyword.py kwlist (31, `print` among them); the grammar follows Grammar/Grammar file_input..print_stmt..atom/trailer/arglist.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# py2-int-print (LANG84 phase 7c slice 1) as this release's grammar admits
# it. The release's own rules, from the tag's Grammar/Grammar:
#
#   file_input : (NEWLINE | stmt)* ENDMARKER
#   simple_stmt: small_stmt (';' small_stmt)* [';'] NEWLINE
#   small_stmt : expr_stmt | print_stmt | ...
#   print_stmt : 'print' ( [ test (',' test)* [','] ] |
#                          '>>' test [ (',' test)+ [','] ] )
#   arith_expr : term (('+'|'-') term)*
#   term       : factor (('*'|'/'|'%'|'//') factor)*
#   factor     : ('+'|'-'|'~') factor | power
#   power      : atom trailer* ['**' factor]
#   trailer    : '(' [arglist] ')' | ...
#   atom       : '(' [testlist] ')' | NAME | NUMBER | ...
#
# Rule names follow code/grammars/python/python3.12.grammar (LANG84 C8), as
# py-int-print's pairs do; `print_stmt` is the one rule Python 2 adds
# (python-iir-compiler PROFILE_RULES lists it for the py2 profile).
#
# Narrower than Python on purpose (parse errors here, valid there): the
# `print >>file` form, every other statement, `**`, `~`, comparisons
# (including `<>`) and boolean operators, subscripts and attributes, tuples
# and `()`, keyword and starred arguments, backquotes, and every compound
# statement.
# Admitted here and refused by the compiler (`Unsupported`): `print a, b`
# and `print a,` (softspace; see LANG84 phase 7c slice 1), a bare
# expression statement, a name, and a call (Python 2's `print` is not a
# function, so every call is outside the subset).
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

file        = { NEWLINE | statement } ;
statement   = simple_stmt ;
simple_stmt = small_stmt { SEMICOLON small_stmt } [ SEMICOLON ] NEWLINE ;
small_stmt  = print_stmt | expression ;
print_stmt  = "print" [ expression { COMMA expression } [ COMMA ] ] ;

expression  = arith ;
arith       = term { ( PLUS | MINUS ) term } ;
term        = factor { ( STAR | SLASH | FLOOR_DIV | PERCENT ) factor } ;
factor      = ( PLUS | MINUS ) factor | primary ;
primary     = atom { suffix } ;
suffix      = LPAREN [ arguments ] RPAREN ;
arguments   = argument { COMMA argument } [ COMMA ] ;
argument    = expression ;
atom        = INT | NAME | paren_expr ;
paren_expr  = LPAREN paren_body RPAREN ;
paren_body  = expression ;
